From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 09:27:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: drive presentation from the OHOS display vsync

Replace the default timer refresh driver with a per-WebView
VsyncRefreshDriver backed by ohos_vsync::NativeVsync. Each built WebView
owns its OH_NativeVSync handle, so the subscription is released when the
WebView is destroyed, and vsync callbacks are requested on demand (only
when Servo observes the next frame), so an idle or absent WebView drives
no frames. Verified on the rk3568: a CSS animation advances smoothly.

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_vsync.py on a device.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
---
